*** merge_relate.pgm — Epiora v1.1 Task 3 reference program.
*** RELATE one-to-many then FREQ: Nutrition1 has 3 patients keyed PatientID
*** ("1","2","3"); all 11 PatientVisits2 rows carry VisitPatientID "1", so a
*** MATCHING relate expands patient 1 to 11 rows and ALL adds the two
*** unmatched parents. MERGE writes into the destination table (the
*** current-read file), so this program runs on a scratch copy
*** (@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb): the PatientID::VisitPatientID merge has 11
*** duplicate source keys all updating destination row "1", and the
*** GlobalRecordId::GlobalRecordId merge has no destination match so all 11
*** source rows insert. MERGE's APPEND/UPDATE/RELATE option word is not
*** usable in 7.2.7.0 (SetMergeOpt reads past the token's children — a
*** hang-producing exception), so only the default match-or-insert merge
*** path is pinned. Pins spec §15.2: RELATE one-to-many then FREQ, MERGE
*** with duplicate keys.
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
ROUTEOUT "@OUTPUT_HTML@" REPLACE
DISPLAY TABLES
LIST PatientID LastName FirstName
RELATE PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID
LIST PatientID VisitPatientID Name HeightInches
FREQ PatientID
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
RELATE PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID ALL
LIST PatientID VisitPatientID HeightInches
FREQ VisitPatientID
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
MERGE '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
LIST PatientID GlobalRecordId
MERGE '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':PatientVisits2 GlobalRecordId::GlobalRecordId
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
FREQ PatientID
CLOSEOUT
QUIT
